  "policy": [
    "Skill archetypes are universal definitions; territory-specific rendering is instance metadata and never forks the shared identity.",
    "Every rendered skill building is a local instance owned by one project or employer capital even when the same archetype appears more than once.",
    "Authored world anchors spread project cities across their QA allocations and are never inferred from a tiny radial offset.",
    "Skill footprints remain at project-building parity so the shared archetypes read as buildings instead of map pins.",
    "The capital campus contains one local instance of every NinjaOne skill archetype while each project city keeps only its supported skills."
  ],
